      'Suppose your goal is to feel healthier by the summer. Nobody can measure “feel healthier” directly every morning, so you choose something you can measure that you believe drives it — say, resting heart rate below 60 beats per minute. That number is still a single snapshot, and a snapshot does not tell you whether you will make it. What tells you is the trend: the weekly average has fallen from 72 to 66 in six weeks, and if it keeps falling at that rate you will cross 60 with time to spare. If it stalls at 64 in week eight you know early, while there is still time to change your training.',
