      'The margin arithmetic for month 9. TPM-001 (lower is better): threshold 20 min, CBE 18.0 min, so the margin against the CBE — the value the reference records — is 20 − 18.0 = 2.0 min. The month-9 estimate comes from a full-pack charge test on a production-representative pack — the end item, where month 6 rested on a bench test of one module, a surrogate — so the contingency falls from 0.8 to 0.6 min: WCE = 18.0 + 0.6 = 18.6 min and the DoD margin is 20 − 18.6 = 1.4 min (R44 p.117). TPM-002 (lower is better): 65 − 63.5 = 1.5 dBA against the CBE, but the estimate is a prediction with no measurement yet, so the contingency is 1.0 dBA: WCE = 64.5 dBA, margin 0.5 dBA. TPM-003 (higher is better): 23.0 − 20 = 3.0 percentage points against the CBE; contingency 1.5 for end-of-life cell uncertainty gives WCE = 21.5 % and margin 1.5 points. None of the three meets its objective yet (15 min, 62 dBA, 25 %).',
